{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1794280265485961002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"alphabetic-reluctant-dore","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"04f3ad8a5236cf8f3de470a4c43c97b23192d56d49556c2ca26a257e62c18f09","event_uuid":"eabac993-21cb-4c10-8429-5da796bb317d","position":{"commit_sha":"7f4e64a331ded1f62da4acc25e73516e4f5a572b","position":"1794280246679481001-eabac993-21cb-4c10-8429-5da796bb317d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"c5f9c3f1a1416a527055a0bdd5a8cdf3a6cf1b3bc2e9359cb7e932df332e47a5","event_uuid":"f6a2bdb1-38a2-4433-8087-b85681be9330","position":{"commit_sha":"531efd9ad9e05c7dc4853198c15f88cd8937b4c8","position":"1794280265485961001-f6a2bdb1-38a2-4433-8087-b85681be9330"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1794280246679481001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f6a2bdb1-38a2-4433-8087-b85681be9330","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"81a1-0fc3-496d-4a00"}],"description":"## Problem\n\n`tests/unit/test_review_bot.py::test_shutdown_drains_an_in_flight_reconciler_review` fails intermittently in CI's `pytest (ubuntu-latest, py3.12)` cell:\n\n```\nAssertionError: the reconciler's review never fired within 3.0s — the probe is not wired\nassert []\ntests/unit/test_review_bot.py:981\n```\n\n`_await_probe` (`tests/unit/test_review_bot.py:966-981`) polls a worker-thread probe against a fixed 3.0 s wall-clock cap. The same run also logs `OSError: [Errno 98] ... address already in use`.\n\n## Evidence (measured 2026-11-09)\n\n- Failed on two unrelated changes in the last 40 failed CI runs since 2026-10-25: run 42742825985 (2026-11-10 02:26 UTC, Gerrit change 3341, which only edits eval-spec `model:` lines and one evidence-kind test) and run 41638314556 (2026-11-03 12:44 UTC).\n- Not reproduced locally on change 3341's tree (macOS, py3.12.14): 0 of 30 isolated runs and 0 of 6 whole-file `-n 4` runs failed.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe test should pass or fail on the shutdown-drain behaviour it checks, not on host load. Whether the 3.0 s cap, the reconciler's start path, or the port collision is the cause is untested; a deterministic reproduction should come first (AGENTS.md: a flaky test is a bug to root-cause, not a retry).\n\n## Impact\n\nIt blocks Verified +1 on change 3341, so that change can't land until this is fixed or an operator authorizes a recheck.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"ccf7-9899-ded6-4313","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Flaky CI test: test_shutdown_drains_an_in_flight_reconciler_review times out at its fixed 3.0s probe cap","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["eabac993-21cb-4c10-8429-5da796bb317d","f6a2bdb1-38a2-4433-8087-b85681be9330"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794280265485961002,"uuid":"7f5daf8b-8aba-4ed3-b79d-364b2d0d2313"}